\fs32\b Files\b0\fs20\par
\par
The File commands are used to create, open and save WinBMD2 transcription files.\par
\par
\fs24\b Starting a new batch\b0\fs20\par
To begin a new transcription, start a new batch and complete the Header Form with the details of the index page you are going to transcribe.\par
\par
When the required information has been entered, click Start batch and the transcription grid will be prepared for the new batch.\par
\par
See The Header Form topic for an explanation of the information entered when starting a batch.\par
\par
\fs24\b Opening an existing batch\b0\fs20\par
Use Open existing batch when you want to continue working on a transcription which has already been saved.\par
\par
You can also open an existing batch directly from the Header Form instead of starting a new one.\par
\par
When the file is opened, WinBMD2 restores the transcription and the information stored with it so that work can continue.\par
\par
\fs24\b Saving your work\b0\fs20\par
Save the transcription regularly while you are working on it. This ensures that the transcription file contains your latest changes and can be reopened later if you need to stop before completing the batch.\par
\par
Saving does not require the transcription to be complete or verified. You can save your work and return to it later.\par
\par
\fs24\b The Output folder\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 stores transcription files intended for submission to FreeBMD in its Output folder.\par
\par
A shortcut to the WinBMD2 Output folder is provided so that these files can be found easily outside WinBMD2.\par
\par
\fs24\b Editing the header\b0\fs20\par
If the batch information needs to be changed after a transcription has been started, use Edit Header.\par
\par
The Header Form will be displayed with the current information, allowing the appropriate details to be corrected.\par
\par
See The Header Form topic for more information.\par
